{"name":"Fragrant Orchid","hex":"#dcbdc8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragrant orchid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An orchid, Gymnadenia conopsea"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrant_orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gymnadenia conopsea","blocks":[{"text":"Gymnadenia conopsea, commonly known as the fragrant orchid or chalk fragrant orchid, is a herbaceous plant of the family Orchidaceae native to northern Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg/330px-M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnadenia_conopsea"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg/500px-M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg/1280px-M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg/500px-M%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM%C3%BCcken-H%C3%A4ndelwurz_Gymnadenia_conopsea.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/0rchideen_04.jpg/500px-0rchideen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/0rchideen_04.jpg/1280px-0rchideen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/0rchideen_04.jpg/500px-0rchideen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gymnadenia conopsea flowers with nectar-filled spur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A0rchideen_04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Gymnadenia_conopsea_-_Harilik_k%C3%A4oraamat_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg/500px-Gymnadenia_conopsea_-_Harilik_k%C3%A4oraamat_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org